cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. It is a research prototype, not for clinical use."
title: "NurseGlance: a nurse-centered, FHIR-based ICU handoff dashboard"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baabdallah
    given-names: Ibrahim
version: 1.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibrahimbaabdullah-jpg/nurseglance"
url: "https://ibrahimbaabdullah-jpg-nurseglance-streamlit-app-uvwgbm.streamlit.app/"
abstract: >-
  An open-source research prototype that shows ICU patients from the MIMIC-IV
  Clinical Database Demo on FHIR in two ways: a tabbed EHR-style control view
  and an organ-system nurse handoff view. It includes a FHIR R4 pipeline with
  LOINC mapping, a crossover study mode with event logging, SUS and NASA-TLX,
  a scripted task analysis, a heuristic evaluation, and a proposed crossover
  usability-study protocol. Click and time results are design-level estimates,
  not measurements of nurses.
keywords:
  - HL7 FHIR
  - MIMIC-IV
  - intensive care unit
  - nursing handoff
  - clinical dashboard
  - EHR usability
  - information visualization
